# Secrets and local configuration
framework/.env
*.secret
*.key
# Python and local tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
# Raw datasets and generated benchmark outputs
datasets/real_infra_runs/
datasets/analysis_results.json
datasets/metadata/source_validation_report.json
datasets/metadata/*.json
# Benchmark runs: excluded by default, because a run directory accumulates
# superseded attempts and re-runs that the manuscript does not cite.
datasets/benchmark_results_*.json
# ...except the ONE run the manuscript cites. revision_stats.py,
# deployment_cost.py and the CI assertion all read this file, so excluding it
# made the repository unable to reproduce its own reported numbers: a reader
# would clone the code and find its only input missing. Negative pattern, so it
# must come after the exclusion above to take effect.
!datasets/benchmark_results_20260219_054729.json
# Generated figures and local logs
*.pdf
*.png
*.log
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.out
*.toc

# Raw datasets and generated benchmark outputs
#
# The five public source datasets ARE tracked, through Git LFS (see
# .gitattributes). creditcard.csv is 144 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# limit for ordinary git, so LFS is the only way it can live in the repo.
# Archives are never tracked: the release bundle is re-downloadable.
#
# Caveat: LFS download bandwidth is metered against the repository owner and
# resets monthly (10 GiB on Free and Pro alike; CI downloads count, so about
# 20 full fetches a month fit). The `datasets-v1` release asset is the
# unmetered path and is what CI uses.
datasets/sources/**/*.zip
datasets/sources/**/*.xlsx
*.tar.gz
datasets/raw_tables/**/*.zip
datasets/real_infra_runs/
datasets/analysis_results.json
datasets/metadata/source_validation_report.json
datasets/metadata/*.json

# The five public source datasets ARE tracked, through Git LFS -- see
# .gitattributes. creditcard.csv is 144 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit
# for ordinary git, so LFS is the only way it can live in the repository at all.
# Archives are never tracked: the release bundle is re-downloadable.
#
# Caveat for the repository owner: LFS download bandwidth is metered against the
# owner's allowance and resets monthly (10 GiB on Free and Pro alike, and CI
# downloads count), so roughly 20 full fetches a month fit inside it. The
# `datasets-v1` release asset is the unmetered path, and is what CI uses.
datasets/sources/**/*.zip
datasets/sources/**/*.xlsx
datasets/raw_tables/**/*.zip
*.tar.gz
